# Devices no driver serves, on purpose or for now (D171, driver(6)): what a
# board's description lists that no `driver` record matches. A check over
# each board (vx dtc --check, BoardCheckTests) takes an enabled device
# that neither a driver nor one of these covers as a mistake, so a new
# device a board brings is read once, and a record here says why it has no
# driver, which is the first line of its driver's notebook when one comes.
# A record here goes when a driver's record matches its devices: the
# check fails a device both cover.

# The CIX Sky1 (docs/boards/orangepi-6-plus).

leave sky1-cpus
match acpi ACPI0007
match acpi ACPI0010
reason processors and their containers: the kernel brings CPUs up from the MADT and power(8) reads their CPPC

leave sky1-pci-root
match acpi PNP0A08
reason a PCI root bridge: devmgr enumerates its buses itself, over the MCFG's ECAM

leave sky1-platform-acpi
match acpi ACPI0003
match acpi PNP0C02
match acpi PNP0C0A
match acpi PNP0C0C
match acpi MSFT0101
match acpi GPIT0000
reason ACPI's own devices (the AC adapter, a resource reservation, the battery, the power button, the TPM, a GPIO test device): nothing a driver is needed for yet

leave sky1-uart
match acpi ARMH0011
reason PL011 UARTs besides the console, which the kernel drives itself; no driver yet

leave sky1-dsd-compatible
match acpi PRP0001
reason devices named only by a _DSD compatible (sound card parts and the like): no driver yet

leave sky1-serial-devices
match acpi SPBD0000
match acpi SPT0002
match acpi RTL5682
match acpi CIXH200D
match acpi CIXH2001
match acpi CIXH2011
reason devices on SPI and I2C buses, the SPI and PWM controllers: no driver yet

leave sky1-platform-mailbox
match acpi CIXHA001
match acpi CIXHA004
match acpi CIXHA005
reason mailboxes and shared memory: scmi(3) is given their pages through its links, and no driver serves them for themselves yet

leave sky1-platform-misc
match acpi CIXA1019
match acpi CIXH1006
match acpi CIXH1007
match acpi CIXHA000
match acpi CIXHA010
match acpi CIXHA012
match acpi CIXHA013
match acpi CIXHA014
match acpi CIXHA015
match acpi CIXHA016
match acpi CIXHA017
match acpi CIXHA018
match acpi CIXHA019
match acpi CIXHA022
match acpi CIXHA023
match acpi CIXHA024
match acpi CIXHA026
reason CIX platform devices (timers, DMA engines, clock and reset units, power management, the EC, TEE, hardware monitor, muxes): no driver yet

leave sky1-usb
match acpi CIXH2030
match acpi CIXH2031
match acpi CIXH2032
match acpi CIXH2033
match acpi CIXH2034
reason the parts of USB the xhci host doesn't cover (hubs, controller cores, PHYs, Type-C ports): no driver yet

leave sky1-pcie
match acpi CIXH2020
match acpi CIXH2023
reason PCIe controllers and ports: devmgr enumerates what is behind them, and no driver for the controllers themselves yet

leave sky1-video-camera
match acpi CIXH3010
match acpi CIXH3020
match acpi CIXH3021
match acpi CIXH3023
match acpi CIXH3024
match acpi CIXH3025
match acpi CIXH3026
match acpi CIXH3027
match acpi CIXH3028
match acpi CIXH3029
match acpi CIXH302A
match acpi CIXH302B
reason the video codec, the ISP and the camera's parts: no driver yet (the roadmap's V6f)

leave sky1-npu
match acpi CIXH4000
match acpi CIXH4010
reason the NPU and its cores: no driver yet (the roadmap's V6f)

leave sky1-display-parts
match acpi CIXH5001
match acpi CIXH5040
match acpi CIXH5041
reason the GPU's power holder and the eDP panel and its backlight: no driver yet, mali(3) and dptx(3) serve the GPU and the transmitters

leave sky1-audio
match acpi CIXH6000
match acpi CIXH6010
match acpi CIXH6011
match acpi CIXH6020
match acpi CIXH6060
match acpi CIXH6061
match acpi CIXH6062
match acpi CIXH6070
reason audio: the DSP, I2S ports, HDA, the audio subsystem's clock and reset and the sound card: no driver yet

leave sky1-ethernet
match acpi CIXH7020
reason the Ethernet MACs: no driver yet

leave sky1-no-id
match acpi-path \_SB_.TZ*
match acpi-path \_SB_.*.PPRS
match acpi-path \_SB_.*.PRS*
match acpi-path \_SB_.*.PHY*
match acpi-path \_SB_.PCP*.PX*
match acpi-path \_SB_.*.CRE*
match acpi-path \_SB_.UCP*.U*P
match acpi-path \_SB_.U3P4.USB*
reason devices with no hardware id, each a part of another's description: thermal zones (devmgr reads them for `thermal`), power-resource holders (its power(8) path evaluates them), PHYs, ports and cores of the device above

# IOMMU units the kernel owns whole: no device holds their registers.

leave sky1-smmu-pcie
match iommu b010000
reason the PCIe SMMUv3, left enabled by firmware and taken over by the kernel (D126); the tables give it no supply of its own

leave sky1-smmu-display
match iommu b1b0000
reason the display SMMUv3, in the display's power domain; the tables give it no supply of its own, and the supply leases (D169) are what keep a provider from cutting it under a master

# The Orange Pi RV2 (docs/boards/orangepi-rv2).

leave rv2-syscon
match dt spacemit,k1-syscon-rcpu
match dt spacemit,k1-syscon-rcpu2
match dt spacemit,k1-syscon-mpmu
match dt spacemit,k1-syscon-apbc2
reason register blocks of the K1's other system controllers, which devices' syscon links name; k1-syscon(3) serves the APMU, the APBC and the PLLs only, and no driver serves these yet

leave rv2-dma
match dt spacemit,k1-pdma
reason the K1's peripheral DMA engine: no driver yet

leave rv2-uart
match dt spacemit,k1-uart
reason the console's UART, driven by the kernel; no driver for the K1's others yet

leave rv2-qspi
match dt spacemit,k1-qspi
reason the K1's QSPI controller: no driver yet

leave rv2-leds
match dt gpio-leds
reason the board's LEDs: no driver yet
